timestamp=2026-11-09T09:02:33.085Z level=INFO run=7904429e message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# So period boundaries are anchored to Tuesdays (the weekday of earliest record). The counts are different from pure calendar month groupings. Also the question says \"billing period for all employees starts on the same day of the week inherited from the dataset's earliest record. On that day, employees are required to appear at the workplace to collect their salary.\" This strongly suggests the billing period is the period starting on that weekday. And \"for each month, the billing period...\" could mean for each billing period (monthly cycle) — but called \"month\" in the context. Also the answer should give salaries \"for every month\" (billing month). We need to identify which billing month each period corresponds to. Maybe by the month of the start date, or the dominant month? For example, period starting 2025-03-04 covers mostly March — that’s the March billing month. That matches.\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
