timestamp=2026-11-09T09:08:37.868Z level=INFO run=7904429e message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# No zero hours rows for this employee in period 2. Let us look more broadly at what gives +500 to 65020111422 period 2 in our implementation.\n# Maybe there is a row we are including that has malformed tasks but we \"fixed\" in a way that adds extra task value? Or maybe the 500 comes from a specific task ID? For example, task with pay_per_completion 500?\n# Let us look at the rows in period 2 again and also check if any of the task IDs in the raw strings correspond to a task worth 500 that we might be mis-parsing.\ntasks = {}\nimport csv\nwith open('/app/dataset/tasks.csv') as f:\n    reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n    for row in reader:\n        tasks[str(row['task_id'])] = float(row['pay_per_completion'])\n\n# look for any task worth 500\nfor k,v in tasks.items():\n    if v == 500:\n        print(k, v)\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
