timestamp=2026-11-09T09:09:04.900Z level=INFO run=7904429e message=evaluated permission=bash pattern="python3 << 'PY'\n# Earlier when I manually calculated for 834 in period 2, I got:\n# \"834 2025-05-27 00:00:00 hrs=7.0 tasks=[] b=0 total=189.0\"\n# That was because I parsed with ast.literal_eval directly and got tasks as empty or failed? Let us see what I did.\n# In that manual calc, I did: tl = ast.literal_eval(tstr); b = sum(tasks.get(str(t), 0) for t in tl)\n# For \"561]\" (raw), ast.literal_eval will fail. So tl becomes [] (empty list) in the except branch. That’s why I got b=0 and tasks=[].\n# But actually the correct parsed task is [561] giving bonus 500. So my previous manual \"correct\" calculation was wrong because I didn’t apply the same robust parsing as we need to.\n# Our implementation with proper parsing will get b=500 for row 834. That gives extra 500 in period 2.\n# So total becomes 9922 + 500 = 10422. That matches our answer [5706, 14608, 10422, 11766] for period 2 = 10422. Correct!\nPY" action.permission=* action.action=allow action.pattern=*
